{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;<strong>8AM: The Warehouse</strong>&quot; traps the player inside a vast logistics warehouse in the dead of night. Conveyor belts hum, forklifts idle in the dark, and the fluorescent lights buzz like insects. A few workers remain, finishing late shifts among endless rows of crates and metal shelves \u2014 but something feels wrong. Their movements are repetitive, mechanical\u2026 and not everyone who started the night is still accounted for.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >From your security booth, you watch dozens of cameras covering loading bays, corridors, and storage aisles. A worker stands motionless beside a stack of boxes for minutes. Another seems to vanish between camera feeds. Machinery powers on by itself. The intercom crackles with fragments of whispered instructions you never gave.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your task is simple: monitor the warehouse until 8:00 a.m., report anomalies, and keep the operation running. But as time drags on, the system begins to break. Footage desynchronizes. People appear in places they couldn\u2019t reach. A forklift drives itself. Somewhere beyond the security glass, footsteps echo \u2014 heavier than human.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every hour blurs the line between fatigue and hallucination. Is it stress, or something else moving among the pallets? The cameras start showing the same frames over and over, except for one detail that keeps changing: the number of workers left.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;<strong>8AM: The Warehouse</strong>&quot; is a psychological surveillance horror about repetition, routine, and the quiet collapse of reason under artificial light. The night shift never really ends \u2014 it just resets.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4122830?t=1773854689","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4122830?t=1773854689","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4122830/9568a2da3491a2a3181ac47165d70298427de682/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1773854689","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4122830/9568a2da3491a2a3181ac47165d70298427de682/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1773854689","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[2,5],"notes":"This game contains disturbing themes and imagery. It includes depictions of blood, violent acts, and death, as well as psychological horror elements such as fear, tension, and mental distress. Some scenes feature suicide, mutilation, or grotesque violence.\r\n\r\nThere are no sexual acts, nudity, or depictions of sexual assault. The game does not glamorize crime or violence."},"detailed_description":"<h1>JOIN US ON DISCORD!</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4122830/extras/d3a7f6fe24f866f665ad55b3bb531af0.avif?t=1773854689\" width=616 height=200 /></span></p></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;<strong>8AM: The Warehouse</strong>&quot; traps the player inside a vast logistics warehouse in the dead of night. Conveyor belts hum, forklifts idle in the dark, and the fluorescent lights buzz like insects. A few workers remain, finishing late shifts among endless rows of crates and metal shelves \u2014 but something feels wrong. Their movements are repetitive, mechanical\u2026 and not everyone who started the night is still accounted for.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >From your security booth, you watch dozens of cameras covering loading bays, corridors, and storage aisles. A worker stands motionless beside a stack of boxes for minutes. Another seems to vanish between camera feeds. Machinery powers on by itself. The intercom crackles with fragments of whispered instructions you never gave.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your task is simple: monitor the warehouse until 8:00 a.m., report anomalies, and keep the operation running. But as time drags on, the system begins to break. Footage desynchronizes. People appear in places they couldn\u2019t reach. A forklift drives itself. Somewhere beyond the security glass, footsteps echo \u2014 heavier than human.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every hour blurs the line between fatigue and hallucination. Is it stress, or something else moving among the pallets? The cameras start showing the same frames over and over, except for one detail that keeps changing: the number of workers left.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;<strong>8AM: The Warehouse</strong>&quot; is a psychological surveillance horror about repetition, routine, and the quiet collapse of reason under artificial light. The night shift never really ends \u2014 it just resets.</p>","developers":["David Gallardo"],"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Casual","id":"4"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4122830/e9a7e2df809e01dddb1ccb48c481b0420738ff96/header.jpg?t=1773854689","is_free":false,"legal_notice":"8AM: The Warehouse \u00a9 2026 HeadArrow Studios All rights reserved.","linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/s